From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Launcher3: the search bar gives the keyboard back

With 0004 the search bar is a text field on the home screen. A tap on it
brings up the keyboard, and only the back key took it away again: a tap
elsewhere on the home screen left it up ("the keyboard does not go down if I
tap a blank part of the screen", user, Test V37).

The bar around the field takes the window's first focus, so the field is
edited only once touched: it took the focus when the home screen started, and
then the first touch elsewhere only ended an editing that had not begun.

The field is Launcher's ExtendedEditText now, and is handled as Launcher
handles the text field of a folder being renamed: a touch outside it while it
is being edited hides the keyboard, ends the editing and goes no further (no
app starts by accident). The back key and a search sent with the keyboard's
search key end the editing as well.

